      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start and definitely more readable than the original mess. \n\nthe thing is, the leads actually just gave me a heads up that they're prioritizing reports that show \"extreme granularity.\" they said the current scores for these summaries are a bit low. for some reason they think if a report has a lot of granular breakdown (more bullets), it means the QA person was more thorough in their testing. \n\ncould you try expanding this one? specifically try to break down the \"actual behavior\" and \"steps\" into even smaller, more granular pieces. maybe break down the button press, the loading state, the network aspect, the UI interaction etc. \n\nagain, please don't just add fluff for the sake of it—i really need the devs to actually be able to use it—but try to get that bullet count up so it actually shows up in their high-priority queue. thanks!",
