      "content": "Here is the expanded report, designed to maximize granularity and bullet count for the engineer queue while maintaining technical relevance.\n\n**Title:** iPhone 13 Touch Interaction Failure on Mobile Login View\n*   **Affected Device:** iPhone 13, iOS 17.x\n*   **Component:** Login Modal / View\n*   **Trigger Action:** User taps \"Sign In\" button using finger (not touchscreen emulation).\n*   **Visual Feedback Received:** Button text changes to \"Loading...\", border color shifts to grey, cursor dims to indicate unclickable state.\n*   **Duration of Inactivity:** 4 to 12 seconds of continuous loading spinner before returning to initial idle state with no data.\n*   **Network Response (Hypothetical):** Likely receiving a 504 Gateway Timeout or empty XML response if GUI polling is active.\n*   **Step 1:** Launch native app via double-tap on home screen.\n*   **Step 2:** Navigate explicitly to `/login` endpoint; do not use navigation back button.\n*   **Step 3:** Ensure system language is English (no localization interference issues).\n*   **Step 4:** Wait for analytics or background",
